 25  #c       Santiniketan - 731 235, West Bengal, India                        
 25   C  CIT$NDS 205, 1 (2025)                                                  
 25   c  ABST$Evaluated spectroscopic data and level schemes are presented for  
 25  2c  {+25}N (unobserved), {+25}O, {+25}F, {+25}Ne, {+25}Na, {+25}Mg,        
 25  3c  {+25}Al, {+25}Si, and {+25}P based on the measured decay and nuclear   
 25  4c  reaction studies. This evaluation for A=25 supersedes the earlier one  
 25  5c  by R.B. Firestone (2009Fi05). Overall the decay datasets associated    
 25  6c  with {+25}Ne, {+25}Na, and {+25}Mg remain the same compared with those 
 25  7c  in the previous evaluation, 2009Fi05, however, new |b-n decay datasets 
 25  8c  are added in {+25}Ne along with new reaction datasets almost for all   
 25  9c  of the above mentioned nuclides from older and new references.         
 25  @c  Other highlights of this evaluation are the following:                 
 25  @c  Ground state of {+25}O is neutron unbound. Several new articles        
 25  2c  reported resonance energies of this nuclide, studied using radioactive 
 25  3c  beams, like {+24}O,{+27}Ne, {+26}F, etc. These results have been       
 25  4c  included in this evaluation.                                           
 25  @c  Due to the lack of direct experimental evidence, a tentative (5/2{++}) 
 25  2c  assignment for the ground state and no spin-parity assignments for the 
 25  3c  known excited states of {+25}Si has been adopted in the present        
 25  4c  evaluation.                                                            
 25  @c  In the absence of experimental evidence, tentative (1/2{++})           
 25  2c  assignment has been adopted for the ground state of {+25}P. As         
 25  3c  suggested in 2015Fe02, light-ion scattering experiment in the inverse  
 25  4c  kinematics seems to be a probable probe for investigating the          
 25  5c  low-lying states of {+25}P, which are the mirror analogs of the states 
 25  6c  of {+25}Ne.                                                            
 25   c  CUT$All data received by May 31, 2025 have been evaluated. During this 
 25  2c  evaluation, the NSR database (2014Pr09) was used extensively.          
 25   c  COMM$The internal conversion coefficients (|a) presented in this       
 25  2c  evaluation have been calculated using the computer code BrIcc          
 25  3c  (2008Ki07) based on Band-Raman tables of conversion coefficients.  For 
 25  4c  Log {Ift} and related data, Betashape code (2023Mo21) was used.  In    
 25  5c  cases of weighted averaging of the data, the assigned uncertainty in   
 25  6c  the result is generally not lower than the lowest uncertainty amongst  
 25  7c  the input data points, assuming that the contribution of the           
 25  8c  systematic uncertainty was significant.                                
 25   c  ACKN$This evaluation benefits from earlier evaluations by R.B.         
 25  2c  Firestone (2009Fi05), P.M. Endt (1998En04, 1990En08, 1978En02), and an 
 25  3c  ENSDF update of {+25}N by E.A. McCutchan (Dated 1-May-2022).           
 25  4c  Evaluators are thankful to the compilers of the XUNDL datasets. Also   
 25  5c  the support of Ms. JoAnn Totans, NNDC, for providing secondary and     
 25  6c  other articles is deeply acknowledged. Finally, the evaluators are     
 25  7c  grateful to the reviewer for useful comments and suggestions and to    
 25  8c  Dr. E. McCutchan (NNDC, BNL) for the editorial comments and            
 25  9c  preparation of this manuscript for publication.                        
 25   c  FUND$The work at LBNL was supported by Office of Basic Energy          
 25  xc  Sciences, US Department of Energy, under contract DE-AC02-05CH11231.   
 25  xc  The work at Visva-Bharati University was supported by the IAEA, under  
 25  xc  the research contract no. 26552.  # sbasunia@l                         

