 25O  c  Adapted/Edited the XUNDL dataset compiled by J. Chen (NSCL, MSU),      
 25O 2c  September 22, 2021.                                                    
 25O  c  2019Sw04: Neutron-unbound states were populated via a two-proton       
 25O 2c  knockout reaction with an 101.3 MeV/nucleon {+27}Ne beam produced      
 25O 3c  by fragmentation of a 140 MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary beam from the    
 25O 4c  Coupled Cyclotron Facility at NSCL on a liquid deuterium target.       
 25O 5c  Beam fragments were separated by the A1900 Fragment separator and      
 25O 6c  charged fragments after reaction were re-directed by a large-gap       
 25O 7c  superconducting dipole magnet and identified by energy loss in         
 25O 8c  an ionization chamber and time-of-flight measured using a plastic      
 25O 9c  scintillator. Emitted neutrons were detected by the MoNA-LISA array    
 25O Ac  of 2-m-long plastic scintillator bars. Measured decay energy.          
 25O Bc  Invariant mass spectroscopy was used to reconstruct the decay energy   
 25O Cc  ({+22}O+3n). Deduced evidence for an excited state at E=9 MeV.         
 25O   L 9000                                                                   
 25O  cL E$from the decay energy spectrum constructed using                     
 25O 2cL invariant mass spectroscopy, based on measured neutron energies in a   
 25O 3cL decay sequence of three neutrons. The sum of measured neutron energies 
 25O 4cL of 2.3 MeV, 0.65 MeV and 50 keV is 3 MeV; and the three-neutron        
 25O 5cL separation energy is about 6 MeV (2019Sw04).                           

