 25F     C(26NE,25FG)                  2014VA02,2017VA24         25NDS    202508
 25F   H TYP=FUL$AUT=M. Shamsuzzoha Basunia, Anagha Chakraborty$                
 25F 2 H CIT=NDS 205, 1 (2025)$CUT=31-May-2025$                                 
 25F  c  Includes C({+27}Na,{+25}F|g),({+28}Na,{+25}F|g). Secondary beam also   
 25F 2c  contained {+24}F, {+25}Ne, {+29}Mg, and {+30}Mg (2014Va02).            
 25F  c  2014Va02: {+25}F was produced from fragmentation of {+26}Ne and        
 25F 2c  {+27,28}Na                                                             
 25F 3c  secondary beams, E=54 to 65 MeV/nucleon, on an "active" target         
 25F 4c  of plastic scintillator (thickness=103 mg/cm{+2}), sandwiched by two   
 25F 5c  carbon foils of thickness 51 mg/cm{+2}. {+25}F nuclei were selected by 
 25F 6c  SPEG spectrometer and identified by energy loss, total energy,         
 25F 7c  time-of-flight, and focal-plane position information. Secondary beams  
 25F 8c  of {+24}F, {+25,26}Ne, {+27,28}Na and {+29,30}Mg with energies         
 25F 9c  54-65 MeV/nucleon were obtained from fragmentation of {+36}S primary   
 25F ac  beam, E=77.5 MeV/nucleon, bombarding a carbon target of thickness 348  
 25F bc  mg/cm{+2} at GANIL. Product nuclei were selected by the |a             
 25F cc  spectrometer equipped with a 130 mg/cm{+2} Al wedge at the dispersive  
 25F dc  focal plane. |g rays were detected by an array of 74 BaF{-2} crystals. 
 25F ec  Measured E|g, I|g, particle-|g, particle-|g|g coincidences, deduced    
 25F fc  {+25}F level scheme. Comparison with shell model, and coupled-cluster  
 25F gc  calculations. Plastic scintillator target contained hydrogen as well.  
 25F  c  2017Va24: {+25}F was produced via one-proton knockout reaction from    
 25F 2c  {+26}Ne secondary beams, E=456 MeV/nucleon (at entrance), on a CH{-2}  
 25F 3c  target (thickness=922 mg/cm{+2}). {+26}Ne was produced from            
 25F 4c  fragmentation of {+40}Ar beam, E=490 MeV/nucleon, on a {+9}Be target   
 25F 5c  (thickness=4 g/cm{+2}). Fragments were separated and selected by the   
 25F 6c  fragment separator at GSI facility and identified event-by-event from  
 25F 7c  energy loss and time-of-flight. |g rays were detected by 159 NaI       
 25F 8c  crystals of the 4|p Crystal ball detector. Two pairs of double-sided   
 25F 9c  silicon strip detectors (DSSSD) were placed before and after the       
 25F ac  reaction target to determine the energy loss. Also two scintillation   
 25F bc  fiber detectors (GFIs), composed of 480 fibers and time-of-flight wall 
 25F cc  (TFW) composed of plastic scintillator paddles, were used in           
 25F dc  combination with DSSSD detectors to identify atomic number Z and mass  
 25F ec  number A. Measured {+25}F energy spectrum, E|g, neutron-|g             
 25F fc  coincidences, deduced {+25}F resonance levels. Comparison with shell   
 25F gc  model calculations.                                                    
 25F  c  Other: 2013Va06                                                        
