 25NE c  2025Pe11: Produced from fragmentation of Ar beam, 200 MeV/A, on a      
 25NE2c  carbon target at the FRIB facility; isotopes were separated and        
 25NE3c  selected using the Advanced Rare Isotope Separator and identified      
 25NE4c  event-by-event by ion energy loss and time-of-flight (tof)             
 25NE5c  measurements; |g rays were detected by a subset of the                 
 25NE6c  Hybrid Array of Gamma Ray Detectors (HAGRiD), comprised 10 LaBr{-}3    
 25NE7c  crystals; |b-delayed neutrons were detected using a double wall of 88  
 25NE8c  Versatile Array of Neutron Detectors at Low Energy (a modular array of 
 25NE9c  plastic scintillator detectors); measured |b-n, |b-|g coincidences,    
 25NEac  neutron tof spectrum; deduced neutron unbound excited states of        
 25NEbc  {+25}Ne, I|b from the measured |b-delayed neutron measurements,        
 25NEcc  half-life and beta-delayed neutron emission branching of {+25}F. A     
 25NEdc  total of 1.53 |* 10{+6} {+25}F ions were implanted and 926,000 |b      
 25NEec  decays were detected (61% |b efficiency was achieved). In the beam     
 25NEfc  setting, {+22}Ne, {+24}O, and {+26}F isotopes were also transmitted    
 25NEgc  significantly.                                                         
 25NE c  2005Pa74: Produced by Be({+48}Ca,x), E({+48}Ca)=140 MeV/nucleon.       
 25NE2c  Fragment separator, double sided Si microstrip detector, segmented Ge  
 25NE3c  array. Measured time-of-flight, E|g, I|g, |g|g- and |b|g-coincidence.  
 25NE c  1999Re16: Produced by Ta({+36}S,x), E({+36}S)=2.8 GeV. Magnetic        
 25NE2c  spectrometer (LISE3). E-|DE telescope. Measured time-of-flight, |b|g   
 25NE3c  coincidence.                                                           
