 25NA c  Adapted/Edited the XUNDL dataset compiled by J. Chen (NSCL, MSU),      
 25NA2c  December 8, 2020.                                                      
 25NA c  2020Wi11: {+18}O beam, E=48 MeV, was produced from the TRIUMF-ISAC     
 25NA2c  facility. Targets were a thin and a backed foil of natural carbon.     
 25NA3c  |g rays were detected with the TIGRESS array consisting of 13          
 25NA4c  Compton-suppressed HPGe clovers and charged particles were detected    
 25NA5c  with a 38-element array of CsI(Tl) scintillators. Measured E|g, I|g,   
 25NA6c  |g|g-coin, particle-|g-coin, |g(|q). Deduced excited level energies,   
 25NA7c  spin, parity, lifetimes, |g-ray multipolarities, transition strengths. 
 25NA8c  Shell-model calculations.                                              
 25NA c  Other reactions: {+12}C,{+16}O({+16}O,X) at E=70-130 MeV (1986Ik03)    
 25NA cG E(Y)$New transition (2020Wi11).                                        
 25NA cG RI$Relative intensity with respect to I|g(2419.6|g)=100. In 2020Wi11,  
 25NA2cG relative intensities were reported with respect to I|g(2419.6|g)=1.00. 
 25NA cG M$From |g(|q) (2020Wi11), proposed by the evaluator, except where      
 25NA2cG otherwise noted.                                                       
 25NA cG M(P)$Assignment in 2020Wi11, based on their |g(|q) data.               
 25NA cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies. The bands proposed      
 25NA2cL in 2020Wi11 are labelled as "sequence" in this dataset.                
 25NA3cL Same spin is proposed for two states by the authors doe most of their  
 25NA4cL proposed bands.                                                        
 25NA cL E(X)$Newly identified level in 2020Wi11 compared to the known excited  
 25NA2cL levels of {+25}Na prior to their work.                                 
 25NA cL J$As given in 2020Wi11 based on |g(|q) and |g de-excitation pattern,   
 25NA2cL unless otherwise noted.                                                
 25NA cL J(Z)$From Adopted Levels. In 2020Wi11, it was quoted from the          
 25NA2cL literature.                                                            
 25NA cL T$From DSAM in 2020Wi11. Limit reported to a 90% confidence level.     
