 25AL    26P ECP DECAY (43.6 MS)       2004TH09,1983CA06,2017JA0525NDS    202508
 25AL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=M. Shamsuzzoha Basunia, Anagha Chakraborty$                
 25AL2 H CIT=NDS 205, 1 (2025)$CUT=31-May-2025$                                 
 25AL c  2004Th09: {+26}P isotope produced in fragmentation of {+36}Ar{+18+}    
 25AL2c  ions at E=95 MeV/nucleon on a {+12}C production target. Fragment       
 25AL3c  separation with LISE3 spectrometer at GANIL.                           
 25AL4c  Measured E|g, E(proton), I|g, |g|g, |g|b coin, p|b coin, p|g|b coin,   
 25AL5c  half-life with one segmented Ge clover detector and five Si detectors. 
 25AL c  1983Ca06 (also 1983Ho23, 1984Ca29, 1984CaZV thesis): {+26}P produced   
 25AL2c  and identified in {+28}Si({+3}He,p4n) reaction at E=110-130 MeV at LBNL
 25AL3c  facility. Measured beta-delayed two-proton pp-coin, E(p), half-life,   
 25AL4c  %|ep, %|e2p                                                            
 25AL c  2017Ja05: {+26}P obtained from {+32}S fragmentation from Be({+32}S,X), 
 25AL2c  E=51.3 MeV/nucleon, reaction; isotopes were separated using            
 25AL3c  fragment separator at JINR, Dubna, Russia facility. Fragments were     
 25AL4c  identified by time-of-flight (tof) and energy-loss technique using     
 25AL5c  plastic scintillator and a silicon detector, respectively. Selected    
 25AL6c  fragments were analyzed by Optical Time Projection Chamber (OTPC),     
 25AL7c  filled with 49.5% Ar, 49.5% He, and 1% Co{-2} at atmospheric pressure. 
 25AL8c  Light produced in the gas was recorded by a digital camera (CCD) and a 
 25AL9c  photomultiplier (PMT) connected to an oscilloscope; the combination    
 25ALac  of data from the CCD and the PMT was used to reconstruct particle      
 25ALbc  tracks in three dimensions.                                            
 25ALcc  Setup was tuned for {+27}S ions, but {+26}P was also accepted. In total
 25ALdc  2497 events of {+26}P were identified, of which 2463 events based on   
 25ALec  depth profile were inspected to select decay events.                   
 25ALfc  141 cases of |bp emission is used to reconstruct the emitted proton    
 25ALgc  energy.                                                                
 25AL c  2022Li66: {+26}P were produced from projectile fragmentation of a      
 25AL2c  80.6-MeV/A {+32}S{+-16+} primary beam on {+9}Be target. The projectile 
 25AL3c  fragments were separated using the Radioactive Ion Beam Line in        
 25AL4c  Lanzhou, identified by energy loss and time of flight. Ions were       
 25AL5c  implanted into a silicon array consisting of three DSSD detectors;     
 25AL6c  measured E{-p}, I{-p}, E|g; deduced proton energies and relative       
 25AL7c  intensities.                                                           
 25AL c  2020Li06: {+26}P from fragmentation of {+32}S with E=80.6              
 25AL2c  MeV/nucleon. Reaction products separated and purified by RIBLL1 in     
 25AL3c  Lanzhou. Ions identified by time-of-flight and energy loss.            
 25AL4c  Detection system consisted of three double sided-silicon strip         
 25AL5c  detectors, five Clover-type HPGe detectors, and five quadrant          
 25AL6c  silicon detectors.                                                     
 25AL c  2015Sc16: {+26}P isotope produced in fragmentation of {+36}Ar          
 25AL2c  primary beam, E=150 MeV/nucleon, on a {+9}Be production target.        
 25AL3c  Fragments were separated with A1900 fragment separator at NSCL;        
 25AL4c  implanted in a planar germanium double-sided strip detector (GeDSSD)   
 25AL5c  and surrounded by SeGA array of high purity germanium detectors.       
 25AL6c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g and |g|b coin, deduced proton feedings to
 25AL7c  {+25}Al levels, excitation energy of proton emission level in {+26}Si  
 25AL8c  from Doppler broadening of |g-ray peaks                                
