 25SI c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |s using SeGA array                           
 25SI2c  comprised of 17 high-purity 32-fold segmented Ge detectors at the      
 25SI3c  National Superconducting Cyclotron Laboratory of Michigan State        
 25SI4c  University (MSU). The {+36}Ar primary beam at the energy of            
 25SI5c  150 MeV/nucleon was used. The primary beam impinged on a {+9}Be        
 25SI6c  production target at the midacceptance position of the A1900 fragment  
 25SI7c  separator. The resulting secondary beam of {+26}Si was then steered    
 25SI8c  onto a 376 mg/cm{+2} thick {+9}Be secondary target located at the      
 25SI9c  pivot point of the S800 large acceptance magnetic spectrograph.        
 25SIac  The energy of {+26}Si at the mid-target position was 109 MeV/nucleon.  
 25SIbc  The secondary target was surrounded by the detector array, SeGA.       
 25SIdc  The experimental results were compared with the USDB shell-model       
 25SIec  calculations.                                                          
