 25SI3c  {+9}Be primary target with E=150 MeV/nucleon {+36}Ar primary beam      
 25SI4c  provided by the NSCL cyclotron. Beam fragments were separated by the   
 25SI5c  A1900 separator. Secondary target was a 287 {I3} mg/cm{+2} thick       
 25SI6c  {+9}Be. |g rays were detected with the CAESAR high-efficiency array    
 25SI7c  consisting of 192 CsI(Na) scintillators and in a separate experiment,  
 25SI8c  SeGA array comprised of 32-fold segmented HPGe detectors;              
 25SIac  the reaction residues were analyzed with the S800                      
